<title>ITALY: Italy wants golden share in Stet sell-off.</title>
<headline>Italy wants golden share in Stet sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy wants a golden share in the privatisation of state-controlled telecoms group STET, Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ciampi told reporters: &quot;The golden share is a point we intend to confirm.&quot;</p>
<p>He also said the government wanted to put together a hard core of mainly Italian shareholders in the company ahead of its privatisation.  </p>
<p>&quot;We intend to create a hard core of mainly Italian shareholders who do not have related activities (to telecommunications),&quot; said Ciampi.</p>
<p>The government has approved the merger of Stet with Telecom Italia in preparation for the sale to the public of shares in the merged entity. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
